This commit introduces the `bpf_prog_array_map_clear` function (which was later renamed/generalized to `bpf_fd_array_map_clear`). The function contains the vulnerable loop that iterates over all map entries and deletes them without any rescheduling point (`cond_resched()`): 

c
void bpf_prog_array_map_clear(struct bpf_map *map)
{
	struct bpf_array *array = container_of(map, struct bpf_array, map);
	int i;

	for (i = 0; i < array->map.max_entries; i++)
		prog_array_map_delete_elem(map, &i);
}

This allows a large map to monopolize the CPU during deletion, triggering RCU stalls.
